    "result_text": "There's a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`) which is the whole suite, and it's green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same firstName and lastName, compared case-insensitively \u2014 exposed on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md, the changes were:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount.java` (in `rest/function/owner/`): reads the built `@Val Owner` and the `OwnerRepository`, counts pre-existing owners matching firstName+lastName (trimmed, lower-cased), and sets `owner.setNamesakeCount(count)`. Since the new owner isn't saved yet, `findAll()` naturally excludes it, so a unique name yields 0. This mirrors the existing `AssignCustomerCode`/`CheckHouseholdUnique` steps.\n\n2. **Wired into the POST pipeline** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted `assignNamesakeCount` (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `assignCustomerCode` and `save`.\n\n3. **Persisted field** \u2014 added `namesakeCount` (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) plus getter/setter to the `Owner` model, so the value survives to the later `GET`. MapStruct maps it into `OwnerDto` automatically by name.\n\n4. **API contract** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` integer to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (the source for the generated `OwnerDto`).\n\n5. **Schema/data** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), and appended the extra trailing `NULL` to the positional seed inserts in `hsqldb` and `mysql` `data.sql` (h2/postgres use named-column inserts, so they were unaffected).\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest.coreCountsNamesakes`, which asserts `namesakeCount == 1` for the second of two same-named owners) passes: **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
